  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e0e83d5f270870d48ac3fc737eb0c586, type: 3}
  m_Name: Chargeur
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryTitle: Chargeur
  listOfTextEntry:
  - They could be likened to a "dog" but abnormally large and imposing.
  - Chargers locate their prey through sounds. They seem to lack visual acuity, which
    would explain why they rush towards the last source of noise they detected.
  - During the charge, the kind of drill that serves as their head makes them invulnerable
    to my bullets...
  - "The charge requires an enormous amount of energy, forcing them to \"recharge\"
    between each one.\r"
  - They remain static, searching for the slightest sound that stands out from the
    ordinary.
  - They don't seem to take their environment into account during the charge, I should
    be able to use this to my advantage...
  - Just like the Shooters, the Chargers seem to be lower-tier creatures in the demonic
    hierarchy.
  - Some "live" in packs while others prefer solitude. I still can't figure out what
    really differentiates them, but one thing is for sure, one Charger can hide another!
  - AGGRESSIVE!
  entryVisual: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 413a1a80f5d4d554a8a2c73ea98a7b93, type: 3}
